    "problem_statement": "RetryError.reraise() method not working correctly\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `RetryError.reraise()` method is not behaving as expected. When called, it should re-raise the original exception that caused the retry to fail, but instead it's not raising anything in some cases.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tenacity\n\n@tenacity.retry(stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(2))\ndef failing_function():\n    raise ValueError(\"This should fail\")\n\ntry:\n    failing_function()\nexcept tenacity.RetryError as e:\n    e.reraise()  # This should raise ValueError, but doesn't\n```\n\nAlso reproducible with:\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import Retrying\nimport tenacity\n\nretry = Retrying(reraise=True, stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(2))\n\ndef test():\n    for attempt in retry:\n        with attempt:\n            raise ValueError(\"Should be reraised\")\n\ntest()  # Should raise ValueError but doesn't\n```\n\nThe `reraise()` method should propagate the original exception that caused the retry attempts to fail, but it's not working properly in the current implementation."
  },
